onents/switch-68","page_id":"/docs/components/switch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/switch#accessibility","content":"When `children` is omitted, provide `aria-label` or `aria-labelledby` so the switch has an accessible name"},"1210":{"id":"/docs/components/switch-69","page_id":"/docs/components/switch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/switch#when-to-use-switch","content":"✅ For settings that take effect immediately, without a form submission"},"1211":{"id":"/docs/components/switch-70","page_id":"/docs/components/switch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/switch#when-to-use-switch","content":"✅ For binary on/off preferences (e.g. Wi-Fi, notifications, dark mode)"},"1212":{"id":"/docs/components/switch-71","page_id":"/docs/components/switch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/switch#when-to-use-switch","content":"❌ For selections that require a \"Save\" or \"Submit\" action (use `Checkbox` instead)"},"1213":{"id":"/docs/components/switch-72","page_id":"/docs/components/switch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/switch#when-to-use-switch","content":"❌ For choosing one of several mutually exclusive options (use `Radio` or `SegmentedController` instead)"},"1214":{"id":"/docs/components/switch-73","page_id":"/docs/components/switch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/switch#labeling","content":"Prefer a visible label that names the setting being toggled (e.g. \"Wi-Fi\", not \"On/Off\")"},"1215":{"id":"/docs/components/switch-74","page_id":"/docs/components/switch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/switch#labeling","content":"If the label is omitted, always provide `aria-label`"},"1216":{"id":"/docs/components/switch-75","page_id":"/docs/components/switch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/switch#labeling","content":"Keep labels short and describe the setting, not its current state"},"1217":{"id":"/docs/components/switch-76","page_id":"/docs/components/switch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/switch#props","content":"The `Switch` component has the following props:"},"1218":{"id":"/docs/components/structure","page_id":"/docs/components/structure","type":"page","content":"Structure primitives","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/structure"},"1219":{"id":"/docs/components/structure-0","page_id":"/docs/components/structure","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/structure","content":"Generic structural containers (Content, Header, Footer, ButtonGroup) for composing a component's interior."},"1220":{"id":"/docs/components/structure-1","page_id":"/docs/components/structure","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/structure#hybrid-styling","content":"Hybrid styling"},"1221":{"id":"/docs/components/structure-2","page_id":"/docs/components/structure","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/structure#examples","content":"Examples"},"1222":{"id":"/docs/components/structure-3","page_id":"/docs/components/structure","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/structure#default","content":"Default"},"1223":{"id":"/docs/components/structure-4","page_id":"/docs/components/structure","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/structure#props","content":"Props"},"1224":{"id":"/docs/components/structure-5","page_id":"/docs/components/structure","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/structure#content","content":"Content"},"1225":{"id":"/docs/components/structure-6","page_id":"/docs/components/structure","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/structure#header","content":"Header"},"1226":{"id":"/docs/components/structure-7","page_id":"/docs/components/structure","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/structure#footer","content":"Footer"},"1227":{"id":"/docs/components/structure-8","page_id":"/docs/components/structure","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/structure#buttongroup","content":"ButtonGroup"},"1228":{"id":"/docs/components/structure-9","page_id":"/docs/components/structure","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/structure","content":"**Shared structural containers.** These generic, layout-only components are the building blocks for composing a component's interior (a `Modal`, a card, a panel). They are semantic containers built on `Flex`, so they accept the same layout props (`direction`, `gap`, `alignItems`, `justifyContent`, `padding`, ...)."},"1229":{"id":"/docs/components/structure-10","page_id":"/docs/components/structure","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/structure","content":"**`Content`** — the primary body region (a `<section>`, a column that grows to fill)."},"1230":{"id":"/docs/components/structure-11","page_id":"/docs/components/structure","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/structure","content":"**`Header`** — the top region: title area and optional trailing close (a `<header>` row that spaces its contents apart)."},"1231":{"id":"/docs/components/structure-12","page_id":"/docs/components/structure","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/structure","content":"**`Footer`** — the bottom region: secondary content and/or actions (a `<footer>` row that spaces its contents apart)."},"1232":{"id":"/docs/components/structure-13","page_id":"/docs/components/structure","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/structure","content":"**`ButtonGroup`** — a cluster of related actions, typically inside a `Footer` (an end-aligned, wrapping row with `role=\"group\"`)."},"1233":{"id":"/docs/components/structure-14","page_id":"/docs/components/structure","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/structure#hybrid-styling","content":"Each container works in two modes:"},"1234":{"id":"/docs/components/structure-15","page_id":"/docs/components/structure","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/structure#hybrid-styling","content":"**Standalone** — with no parent context it renders with its own structural defaults and looks the same everywhere."},"1235":{"id":"/docs/components/structure-16","page_id":"/docs/components/structure","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/structure#hybrid-styling","content":"**Adopted** — placed inside a parent that provides its context (`ContentContext`, `HeaderContext`, `FooterContext`, `ButtonGroupContext`), it picks up that parent's styling and spacing automatically. Merge precedence is defaults \\< parent context \\< consumer props (`className` concatenates, handlers chain), via React Aria's `useContextProps`."},"1236":{"id":"/docs/components/structure-17","page_id":"/docs/components/structure","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/structure#hybrid-styling","content":"A parent adopts them by providing the contexts around its children:"},"1237":{"id":"/docs/components/structure-18","page_id":"/docs/components/structure","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/structure#default","content":"The shared structural containers composed together into a card-like layout. Each is a\nplain semantic region here; inside a parent that provides their contexts (e.g. `Modal`)\nthey adopt that parent's spacing automatically."},"1238":{"id":"/docs/components/structure-19","page_id":"/docs/components/structure","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/structure#props","content":"`Content`, `Header`, `Footer`, and `ButtonGroup` each accept all `Flex` layout props."},"1239":{"id":"/docs/components/tag","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","type":"page","content":"Tag","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/tag"},"1240":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-0","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag","content":"Non-interactive labels that highlight statuses and categories."},"1241":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-1","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/tag#installation","content":"Installation"},"1242":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-2","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/tag#examples","content":"Examples"},"1243":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-3","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/tag#default","content":"Default"},"1244":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-4","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/tag#emphasis","content":"Emphasis"},"1245":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-5","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/tag#sizes","content":"Sizes"},"1246":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-6","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/tag#inline","content":"Inline"},"1247":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-7","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/tag#high-contrast","content":"High Contrast"},"1248":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-8","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/tag#with-icon","content":"With Icon"},"1249":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-9","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/tag#indicator","content":"Indicator"},"1250":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-10","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/tag#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"1251":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-11","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/tag#screen-readers","content":"Screen readers"},"1252":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-12","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/tag#decorative-icons","content":"Decorative icons"},"1253":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-13","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/tag#indicator-dot","content":"Indicator dot"},"1254":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-14","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/tag#best-practices","content":"Best Practices"},"1255":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-15","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/tag#when-to-use","content":"When to Use"},"1256":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-16","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/tag#when-not-to-use","content":"When Not to Use"},"1257":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-17","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/tag#props","content":"Props"},"1258":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-18","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#default","content":"A minimal tag with the default emphasis and size."},"1259":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-19","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#emphasis","content":"Nine emphasis options are available. Choose the one that fits the visual tone of your context."},"1260":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-20","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#sizes","content":"Choose a size that fits the surrounding content. Smaller tags work well in compact layouts like tables; larger tags suit headings or hero sections."},"1261":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-21","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#inline","content":"Use `design=\"inline\"` to embed a tag within a sentence. The background and border are removed so the tag blends into the text flow."},"1262":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-22","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#high-contrast","content":"A bolder color treatment for when tags need to stand out more - for example, on colored backgrounds."},"1263":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-23","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#with-icon","content":"Icons reinforce the tag's meaning at a glance. Add an `Icon` as a child - it inherits the tag's color and scales with its size."},"1264":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-24","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#indicator","content":"A minimal style that pairs a small colored dot with a neutral background. Well suited for dense layouts like tables or dashboards where multiple tags in close proximity would otherwise compete for attention."},"1265":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-25","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#screen-readers","content":"Tags are `<span>` elements with no special ARIA role. Screen readers announce the tag's text as part of normal page content — no extra markup is needed."},"1266":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-26","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#decorative-icons","content":"Icons passed as children must include `aria-hidden=\"true\"` so they are skipped by screen readers. The text label is the sole carrier of meaning."},"1267":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-27","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#indicator-dot","content":"The colored dot is decorative and invisible to screen readers. The text label must convey the status on its own — never rely on the dot alone to communicate meaning."},"1268":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-28","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#best-practices","content":"Use the indicator style in dense layouts like tables and dashboards. Use the filled style when the tag is a prominent, standalone element on a card or hero section."},"1269":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-29","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#best-practices","content":"Default to the small size in compact layouts like tables and lists. Use medium or large only when the tag needs to stand out as a primary piece of information."},"1270":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-30","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#best-practices","content":"Use the inline design only within running prose. In grouped or standalone contexts, the filled style provides better visual separation."},"1271":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-31","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#best-practices","content":"Do not stack multiple tags of different emphasis on the same item. Choose the most important one — too many competing labels lose their meaning."},"1272":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-32","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#when-to-use","content":"Showing the status of an item on a card, table row, or list entry (e.g. \"Active\", \"Expired\", \"Pending\")"},"1273":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-33","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#when-to-use","content":"Categorizing or grouping content so users can scan and filter quickly (e.g. \"New\", \"Sale\", \"Beta\")"},"1274":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-34","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#when-to-use","content":"Surfacing metadata about an item (e.g. \"Pro\", \"Free trial\", \"Internal\")"},"1275":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-35","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#when-to-use","content":"Communicating priority or category in project management and collaboration tools (e.g. \"High priority\", \"In review\")"},"1276":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-36","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#when-not-to-use","content":"If users need to click or dismiss it — use a **Button** instead."},"1277":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-37","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#when-not-to-u